    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.98,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 1.3 from 7 h onward, which looks like the reader saturating. At 18 h, a 10x dilution read 0.477, which corresponds to about 4.8 undiluted. A 20x dilution read 0.242, which corresponds to about 4.85. The two dilutions agree with each other, and both are roughly 3.7 times the undiluted reading of 1.32. A real plateau would give about 0.13 at 10x dilution, so the flat reading is a detector ceiling and not a true stationary phase. The 20x reading is the better estimate because it is the least affected by non-linearity. Each dilution had a single replicate, so I have no replicate-based error estimate."
